  "id": "Compound::DB00393 - Gene::775",
  "verbalization": "Nimodipine, a calcium channel blocker, is shown to interact with multiple isoforms of the Cacna1 family, specifically Cacna1f, Cacna1s, and Cacnb1, all of which are involved in high-voltage-gated calcium channel activity. This suggests that Nimodipine may exert its effects by modulating calcium channel function, potentially through binding to these isoforms. The evidence from the three paths indicates a consistent mechanism where Nimodipine interacts with calcium channel subunits, which in turn influence calcium influx and cellular signaling. The high scores in the final scores suggest a strong and reliable interaction, supported by multiple pathways. The overlapping involvement of these isoforms in the same biological process reinforces the likelihood of a mechanistic link between Nimodipine and Cacna1c. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Nimodipine may modulate calcium channel activity, thereby affecting cellular processes associated with high-voltage-gated calcium channels, including those involving Cacna1c.",
